			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1736811">
									

<p>How has the Horizon Initiative not been busted several dozen times by now? Given that they (or even &quot;bad apples&quot; within the organization) are willing to perpetrate a mass murder <em>in the middle of New York state</em>, you would think that people might have noticed them or something. And while they don't concentrate killings in a single area, a moderately intelligent analyst could easily connect the dots. Also, the fact that Jerome's punishment for his role in the attempted is essentially a slap on the wrist, despite his defense being essentially &quot;I was just following orders!&quot; is border-line surreal. Screw external pressures; how the HI is supposed to function with any sort of coherency or organization is beyond me.</p>
<p>The twist ending was quite good, though. Saved it from a downvote to be sure.</p>

