					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/azzleflux" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1444699); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1444699&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608045256" alt="azzleflux" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1444699)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/azzleflux" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1444699); return false;" >azzleflux</a></span> <span class="odate time_1364252886 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">25 Mar 2013 23:08</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1738307">
									

<p>In my headcanon, up to a certain point, their actions were influenced by what was written. However, again, this only works up to a certain point. For example, it was certain that Reggravi would protect the Scribes from a Wolf. Did this necessarily mean that it had to be Project Malleus's &quot;Wolves?&quot; Nope. But that's what happened. Now, there are certain limits (again, this might just be my headcanon for this), mostly that <em>the entire situation is not controlled by the writing. There are many variables.</em></p>
<p>And you have to keep in mind, not every group that is dealt with is anomalous. Just check out <a href="/shepherds">Shepherds</a>. &quot;Possession of a possible artifact&quot; could mean a) they have some anomalous trinket, b) they have a weapon, or c) they might have something, but we don't know, so we should eliminate them before they can use it against us. The people sent into scout didn't really find anything; thus, it was more positive incentive than deterrent for Hunt.</p>

							</div>

								
					
