														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1738490">
									

<p>I think that an artifact clearly indicates a &quot;supernatural&quot; thing in-context. It would be quite silly to call, say, a sawed-off shotgun an &quot;artifact&quot; unless the narrative takes place after some kind of civilization collapse.</p>
<p>Even without &quot;possible supernatural thing on-site&quot; angle, the whole gung-ho approach indicates a rather low level of professionalism which is liable to get an organization in a lot of hot water - just ask Blackwater (badum-tish!). With the supernatural angle in place, it boggles the mind how did those folks live long enough to die by Bundles :)</p>

