<p>The nature of such a dysfunction means that it would be indistinguishable from a sensible organization, right up until the point that it wasn't.</p>
<p>This could very well be the start of an implosion. Demontfort and the afflicted corps he's built up finally reaching that saturation point where irrationality overwhelms good sense en masse. I could see this uncalled for, border-line psychopathic, and ultimately disasterous assault being the pebble that starts an avalanche of official inquiries and psyche evaluations that ends several careers and puts the Wolves back on a relatively rational footing.</p>
<p>Edit: and now I see that Djoric already said basically the same thing, downthread.</p>

